@startuml E3_API_06_LAYERED
title API 06: Prediction and Internal ML APIs (LAYERED view)
!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam ranksep 80
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle


' REST interfaces are grounded in the Express/FastAPI route declarations.
' Layered and MVC are two views of the existing CryptoWeb codebase, not separate implementations.
actor "React client / admin" as Client

component "Core :5000 - Core prediction API\nPOST /api/ml/price-prediction\nGET /api/ml/predictions" as API1 <<REST API>>
component "Core :5000 - Core ML administration\nPOST /api/ml/admin/weekly-train/run" as API2 <<REST API>>
component "Server_3 :4000 - Server_3 ML data API\nGET /v1/ml/candles\nGET /v1/ml/latest_features\nGET /v1/ml/influence_graph" as API3 <<REST API>>
component "ML FastAPI :8000 - Python FastAPI service\nGET /security/anomaly-model\nPOST /security/anomaly-score\nGET /health\nPOST /predict\nPOST /admin/reload" as API4 <<REST API>>

package "Routing and controller layer" {
  component "ml.controller.js (Core)\nmain.py (FastAPI endpoint handlers)\nmlData.controller.js (Server_3)" as Controllers <<Controllers / route handlers>>
}
package "Service and orchestration layer" {
  component "ml.service.js (Core)\nmodel.py / security_anomaly.py (ML)" as Services <<Services / jobs>>
}
database "MongoDB: ml_predictions, signals_ml,\nmarket data; ML model artifacts" as Storage
Client --> API1 : HTTP / JSON
API1 --> Controllers : dispatch
API2 --> Controllers : dispatch
API3 --> Controllers : dispatch
API4 --> Controllers : dispatch
Controllers --> Services : calls (as implemented)
Services --> Storage : reads/writes
Services ..> API4 : POST /predict (service key)
API4 ..> API3 : market data via DataClient (service key)

note bottom of Storage
  Database objects summarized by domain;
  this is an API interaction diagram,
  not a physical ER diagram.
end note
@enduml
